{
  "dom_id": "step-q556431",
  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Between which two consecutive whole numbers does $\\sqrt[3]{20}$ lie?",
  "worked_solution": "To find which two consecutive whole numbers $\\sqrt[3]{20}$ lies between, we can compare $20$ to nearby perfect cubes.\n\n- The closest perfect cube less than $20$ is $8,$ since ${2}^{3}=8.$\n\n- The closest perfect cube greater than $20$ is $27,$ since ${3}^{3}=27.$\n\nThis means $20$ is between $8$ and $27:$\n\n$$\n8<20<27\n$$\n\nTaking the cube root of each part of the inequality gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[3]{8} & <\\sqrt[3]{20}<\\sqrt[3]{27} \\\\ 2 & <\\sqrt[3]{20}<3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\sqrt[3]{20}$ lies between $2$ and $3.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
